    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52607": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Student &amp; Early Alumni Engagement Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005430P Position Title Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement Division/College University Foundation Department Alumni Relations Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The University of Idaho Foundation Alumni Relations team seeks a dynamic leader to serve as Assistant Director of Student & Young Alumni Engagement. Reporting to the Senior Director of Alumni Relations, this role strengthens the lifelong Vandal journey by creating meaningful connections between students, young alumni and the university community. Through leadership of signature traditions and programs like Homecoming, Parent & Family Weekend, Vandal Walk and Graduates of the Last Decade ( GOLD ) engagement, this position fosters pride, belonging and lasting alumni involvement. The Assistant Director will lead student-focused initiatives, supervise a team member and partner across campus to strengthen the Vandal community. Position Overview This position leads engagement initiatives across the student-to-alumni transition, with a focus on career connection, identity development and long-term community building. The Assistant Director works collaboratively with Alumni Relations colleagues, campus partners and other stakeholders to deliver a cohesive, coordinated and meaningful constituent experience. Duties will include: Design and implement initiatives and programming to drive student and young alumni engagement Develop and support career-focused engagement opportunities Cultivate and maintain relationships with campus partners, faculty, student organizations and alumni volunteers Analyze engagement data and feedback Attend university and community events Supervise staff Perform other duties as assigned Unit URL University of Idaho Foundation | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Two years of experience in program development, engagement, event planning or relationship management Experience coordinating and executing programs or initiatives Experience working collaboratively with partners or stakeholders Demonstrated organizational and communication skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines Required Education Bachelor’s degree Required Other Ability to travel Ability to work nonstandard business hours which may include weekends and holidays Must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university vehicles Additional Preferred Demonstrated interest in engagement, events or higher education Demonstrated ability to work independently and contribute strategic ideas Experience in alumni relations, higher education or student engagement Developing programs for students or early career professionals Analyzing participation data and improving programs based on insights Experience in event planning and coordination Supervising staff Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to lift, carry or otherwise move up to 25 pounds Ability to sit at a desk and work on a computer for long periods of time Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $60,000 or higher, commensurate with experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 08/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This in-person position is based in Moscow, Idaho and not offering Visa sponsorship. To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification and current resume no later than September 17, 2026. In your letter of qualifications ( human-resources-letter-of-qualification-template.docx ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu . Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
