    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51310": {
      "title": "Event Safety/Security Officer",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Event Safety/Security Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Event Safety/Security Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002191P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Event Safety/Security Officer Location Moscow Division/College DFA Operations Department Security FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $18.00 per hour or higher depending on experience Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary Must be able to work a non-standard schedule to meet the needs of the department. Work an average of 20 hours a week. Position Responsibilities Position Summary Event Safety/Security Officer provides a multitude of services that provides a safe and secure environment for the university community for events happening throughout campus. This position also plays a key role in establishing and strengthening relationships with on campus and off campus stakeholders through providing exemplary customer service. Responsibilities Job Duty Function Implement event related safety and security tasks at events on campus by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Operating metal detectors and executing the metal detection screening process Conducting alcohol enforcement tasks at events, including verifying age requirements and wrist banding patrons and enforcement of university alcohol policies Enforcing access control enforcement at events by checking credentials, tickets, etc. Enforcing university clear bag requirements and checking bags as necessary Conducting general security patrol at events and reporting any emergencies to the necessary city or state officials Percentage Of Time 40 Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Provide exemplary customer service by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Effectively communicating venue and university policies to guests during screening and alcohol enforcement duties Providing appropriate assistance to guests with disabilities Politely and respectfully directing guests to ensure screening lines moves efficiently Answering guest questions and providing directions within the venue Percentage Of Time 40 Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Contribute to the team effort by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Accepting additional responsibilities and assignments as directed Making recommendations and assisting in the optimum use of university resources Serving as a scheduler for facilities when necessary Percentage Of Time 20 Essential/Marginal Marginal Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Experience: Working in a team environment to accomplish shared goals. Following documented policies and procedures. High School Diploma or equivalent. Due to the duties of this position, successful candidates must be at least 18 years of age. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of safety and security operations best practices 1 year experience as a safety/security officer Experience that shows ability to communicate effectively in oral and in written communication Using common office computer applications including word-processing, spreadsheet, email and browser applications Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to move about and between venues for extended periods of time up to a full day of work. Work inside and outside as required. Posting Information Posting Date 04/14/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed at regular intervals throughout the academic year. In your letter of qualification , using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. The information provided in your letter of qualification will be used to determine eligibility for an interview and demonstrate your communications skills. Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51189 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * The duties of the position require successful candidates to be at least 18 years of age. Do you meet this requirement? Yes No * This position requires experience working in a team environment .  Please describe/explain how you meet this requirement. (Open Ended Question) * This position requires experience following documented policies and procedures.  Please provide examples of how you meet this requirement. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or equivalent? yes no A preferred qualification for this position is knowledge of safety and security operations best practices.  Please explain how you meet this qualification. (Open Ended Question) * After reviewing this position description and qualifications listed, are you willing and able to perform the work requirements of this position? Yes No A preferred qualification is 1 year experience as a safety/security officer.  Please explain how you meet this qualification. (Open Ended Question) Describe how you acquired effective oral and written communication skills. (Open Ended Question) The demands of this position may require the incumbent to work a non standard schedule.  Are you willing to meet this requirement? Yes No What days and hours are you available? (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
