    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52404": {
      "title": "Print Center Assistant Manager",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Print Center Assistant Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Print Center Assistant Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005371P Position Title Print Center Assistant Manager Division/College University Communications & Marketing Department Printing Services Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview This position assists in managing the high-quality production of printed materials that represent University of Idaho, tells the Vandal story and ensures a positive reflection of our brand. This position works collaboratively with the in-house creative team and external clients to ensure products meet or exceed University of Idaho’s quality and standards. Duties may include: Assist with coordinating print and copy projects, ensuring timely and accurate completion Review and prepare job tickets for processing Operate and maintain reprographic, bindery and related equipment Assist with monitoring supplies and inventory management Provide customer service, answering questions and helping resolve issues or requests Assist with processing invoices, transactions and billing as needed Assist with delegating tasks, training and overseeing other employees Other duties as assigned Unit URL https://www.uidaho.edu/newsroom Position Qualifications Required Experience One year operating and maintaining high-speed copiers and bindery equipment One year preparing and outputting digital files to networked printers Using desktop publishing, photo editing, word processing and spreadsheet software Working in a customer service-oriented team to accomplish shared goals Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Additional Preferred Project management experience Records management and retention experience Knowledgeable about digital printing, dye-sublimation and other specialty finishing techniques Experience in a cost recovery (charge back) business model Experience understanding and applying mathematical concepts Understanding of purchasing and procurement processes Experience and knowledge running digital presses and worked with all types of finishing equipment Experience with business management such as preparing invoices for billing; tracking supply costs; establishing price structures to ensure profit and cost-effective structure; analyzing needs and developing and recommending budget and equipment purchases; researching new products and methods to improve production; preparing estimates for clients Quality assurance experience Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to: Lift, carry and or otherwise move material up to 50 pounds Distinguish colors, weights and textures such as with various paper stocks Work in an environment with loud noises and odors Degree Requirement N/A: No degree requirement Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range $27 per hour or higher DOE Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding This position is contingent upon the continuation of work and/or funding. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/15/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To receive first consideration, please submit a current resume and letter of qualification no later than July 30, 2026. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents List of References Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
