    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51661": {
      "title": "Campus Events Team",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Campus Events Team Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus Events Team Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002198P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Campus Events Team Location Moscow Division/College Auxiliary Services Department Administrative Operations FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $13.50 per hour Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary Positions work an average of 10 to 20 hours per week, dependent on Campus Event schedule. Position Responsibilities Position Summary Work under the general direction of the Associate Director of Event Production, assisting in setting-up and supporting public events, athletic events, theater productions or civic activities sponsored by the University of Idaho. Responsibilities Job Duty Function Perform tasks to support events and activities by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Setting up event related equipment such as sound equipment, video systems, lighting, chairs/tables, rigging, portable stage risers, large canopies; Moving/delivering and lifting equipment following standard safety procedures; Operating audio equipment, video systems; Providing excellent customer service. Percentage Of Time 80 Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Maintain a safe and clean working environment by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Following procedures, rules, and regulations, and contributing to the team effort Percentage Of Time 10 Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Maintain good records by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Completing basic forms as required; Completing accurate and timely daily, weekly and other time reports necessary for payroll and billing; Assisting in the planning of future activities by keeping and reviewing records and notes of past events. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Contribute to the team effort by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Performing other duties as assigned by the Campus Events Production Manager. Percentage Of Time 5 Essential/Marginal Marginal Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Must be 18 years of age. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of event-related equipment (such as sound and lighting equipment) and applications; Ability to read and interpret blueprints; Ability to maintain a current, valid driver’s license and meet the university’s driving requirements; Experience operating and maintaining multi-channel audio systems, lighting systems and/or video equipment; Experience performing up and down rigging; Experience scheduling, coordinating, and supervising staff. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to: Perform rigging and to stand and squat on catwalks and beams 70 feet above floor level; Lift, carry and/or otherwise move 50 lbs; Work off of ladders; work in dusty environments; Work variable schedules including evening, nights, weekends and holidays to meet production deadlines. Posting Information Posting Date 05/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed at regular intervals with positions being filled as needed. Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51651 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/CV Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho D