    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52297": {
      "title": "Pro Shop Assistant",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Pro Shop Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Pro Shop Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002180P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Pro Shop Assistant Location Moscow Division/College Auxiliary Services Department UI Golf Course FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $14.00 - $18.00 per hour, depending on experience Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary Work schedule will vary depending on work load. This position will be scheduled to work as early as 6:00am and as late as 9:30pm, as well as weekends and holidays. Multiple positions will be hired, there is opportunity to work through the summer until the course closes for the season in the fall. Shifts for this position will run up to 10 hours, and generally no shorter than 6 hours. Shop Assistant may be asked to fill in for Outside Service as needed. Position Responsibilities Position Summary Under the direction of the Head Golf Professional, the incumbent performs one or more of the following types of work: Provide excellent customer service by assisting customers to check in to play golf Sells shop merchandise Opens and closes pro shop Keeps pro shop and restrooms tidy Opens and/or closes cash register daily Gathers and cleans range balls Cleans and gases carts Other duties as assigned Responsibilities Job Duty Function Assists in Pro Shop by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Assisting customers; Selling shop merchandise; Assigning golf carts and tee times, starting groups in orderly manner; Opening (as early as 6:00 AM), closing (as late as 9:30 PM) and securing Pro Shop and carts; Keeping shelves stocked and tidy; Keeping work areas clean throughout the shop; Opening and closing cash register, cashing out daily income; Renting golf equipment; Driving golf carts to marshal the course; Park, clean, and gas incoming carts and respond to requests on the course; Gathering and cleaning range balls; Assisting in Inventory control: Maintaining the food area by making coffee, heating sandwiches and cleaning; Clean and supply restrooms. Percentage Of Time 90% Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Contribute to team effort by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Accomplishing duties as assigned. Percentage Of Time 10% Essential/Marginal Marginal Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university vehicles Experience operating a cash register, processing transactions, and handling money Active or previous experience playing the game of golf Due to the duties of this position, successful candidates must be at least 18 years of age Preferred Qualifications Experience operating a cash register, processing transactions, and handling money Experience working in a golf course pro shop or outside services department Experience providing customer service and building good customer relationships Member of PGA or enrolled in PGM program with successful completion of PAT Strong mathematical, verbal, and written communication skills Ability to work well in stressful and fast-paced environments Experience safely operating golf carts Demonstrated reliability and punctuality in previous employment Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to work a flexible schedule including early mornings, weekends, and holidays Posting Information Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis until all positions are filled. Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51019 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/CV Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * It is minimum requirement of this position to possess a valid drivers license.  Do you meet this requirement? Yes No * It is a requirement to have experience playing golf, do you have experience playing the game of golf? Yes No * What days and hours are you available? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have the ability to work a flexible schedule including early mornings, weekends, and holidays? Yes No * This position requires experience operating a cash register, processing transactions, and handling money, do you have this experience? Yes No Please address as many of the preferred qualifications as you are able. (This question is optional but providing an answer may increase your standing in the screening process.) (Open Ended Question) Do you have a job history that shows your reliable and punctual in previous employment? (Open Ended Question) Due to the duties of this position, candidates are required to be at least 18 years of age.  Are you 18 years of age? yes no University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
