    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52468": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist II, UI Foundation",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Accounting Specialist II, UI Foundation Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Accounting Specialist II, UI Foundation Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005387P Position Title Accounting Specialist II, UI Foundation Division/College University Foundation Department University Foundation CFO Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Guided by its mission to inspire, manage and distribute private support to enhance the excellence of the University of Idaho, the UI Foundation strives to elevate the university’s impact and reputation through transformational philanthropy. The Foundation is defined by four core values: Generosity and Curiosity; One Mission One Team; Leadership through Integrity and Accountability; and Dedication to Excellence. By connecting donor generosity with the university’s greatest opportunities, the Foundation helps fuel student success, advance research and innovation and strengthen the University of Idaho’s future. Position Overview The position performs a variety of accounting activities that range in level of complexity from clerical accounting duties such as managing receivables and payables, to more complex duties such as reconciling accounts and resolving accounting problems. Duties may include: Process, update and maintain various routine accounting records and documents Prepare accounting statements, billing documents and financial reports Enter, retrieve and maintain data on computerized accounting system Respond to customer inquiries Reconcile / analyze accounting records for accuracy and completeness Assist with researching and solving accounting problems Assist with determining proper classification and coding of income and expenditures Assist in compliance with local, state, and federal regulations and University policy and procedures Assist customers with University policies and procedures or make referrals as necessary Collect and record payments; issue receipts Prepare and make daily bank deposits and manage change funds Take necessary action to resolve customer problems or discrepancies Interact with internal and external auditors and participate in auditing projects May process, update and maintain various complex transactions Other duties as assigned Unit URL University of Idaho Foundation | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Two years full-time experience providing financial or business process support within established policies and procedures, including interpreting and applying policies and procedures to practical situations. Experience using computerized accounting systems or spreadsheet software to compile financial information, prepare summaries and reports. A Bachelor’s Degree in accounting or finance may substitute for the above work experience Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other None Additional Preferred Experience in a customer service / support role Experience with accounts receivable activities, including the receipt and deposit of funds Using a large integrated database system such as Banner and/or a Constituent Relationship Management ( CRM ) software solution Manipulating database software to store, retrieve, and compile information into report format Written and verbal communication skills Researching and validating constituent information from multiple sources Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range $20.14 per hour or higher, commensurate with experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/28/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is not offering Visa sponsorship. To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification and current resume no later than Aug. 11th. In your letter of qualifications ( human-resources-letter-of-qualification-template.docx ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu . Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52232": {
      "title": "Clinical Psychologist & PsyD Program Faculty",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Psychologist &amp; PsyD Program Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Psychologist & PsyD Program Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001424P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Psychologist & PsyD Program Faculty Advertising Pay Range $86,500 annually or more, depending on experience and education Location Moscow Primary Division/College School of Health and Medical Professions Primary Unit Department of Clinical Medicine Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 6215 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 05/11/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary This non-tenure-track clinical faculty position is a 1.0 FTE joint appointment shared equally between the Department of Health Professions in the School of Health and Medical Professions ( SHAMP ) and the University of Idaho Counseling and Mental Health Center ( CMHC ). The faculty member will hold the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, with an academic home in the Department of Health Professions and will be eligible for promotion to Clinical Associate Professor and Clinical Professor in accordance with university policy. The position includes a 50% commitment to teaching, supervision, scholarship, and related faculty responsibilities in support of the Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) program and a 50% commitment to direct clinical service at CMHC . The faculty member will serve as core faculty in the PsyD program, consistent with APA Commission on Accreditation (CoA) definitions. The faculty member’s academic home will be in the Department of Clinical Medicine within the School of Health and Medical Professions. For matters related to teaching, scholarship, and faculty evaluation, the faculty member will report to the Department Head of Clinical Medicine or their designee. For clinical operations and day-to-day service responsibilities at the Counseling and Mental Health Center ( CMHC ), the faculty member will work under the direction of the CMHC Director or their designee. As a joint appointment, performance evaluations will incorporate input from both units. Clinical faculty positions at the University of Idaho are non-tenure-track and are designed for professional disciplines with strong applied and clinical components. Responsibilities may include teaching, advising, scholarly activity, graduate committee service, and community or professional outreach. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/cogs/shamp https://www.uidaho.edu/student-resources/health-wellness/counseling-mental-health-center Administrative Summary N/A Contingency Description N/A Teaching & Advising 40% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 50% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology or closely related field from an accredited institution. Licensed or License eligible as a clinical psychologist in the State of Idaho Documented training and supervised experience in evidence-based psychological interventions, including a minimum of one year (or equivalent) of applied clinical practice. Documented training and experience in psychological assessment, including administration, scoring, and interpretation of commonly used standardized instruments. Experience teaching and mentoring students, demonstrated through at least one year of graduate-level instruction, supervision, teaching assistantship, or comparable instructional experience in psychology or a related field. Experience delivering clinically effective and ethically sound services, supported by a minimum of one year of direct service experience with college students or a comparable population. Experience with writing and verbal communication skills, demonstrated through professional reports, presentations, or other formal communication products. Experience collaborating across academic and clinical settings, with evidence of interdisciplinary teamwork or coordinated service delivery. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a university counseling center, college mental health setting, or similar integrated training environment. Experience with crisis intervention, outreach, consultation, and brief model therapy. Experience teaching doctoral or graduate students in psychology or a related health profession. Experience supervising practicum students, interns, or other clinical trainees. Experience mentoring dissertation or other student scholarly work. Familiarity with APA accreditation standards, doctoral training, or competency-based clinical education. Knowledge of FERPA , HIPAA , risk management, and documentation standards relevant to higher education clinical settings. Experience conducting psychological assessments, evaluating for autism spectrum disorder, ADHD , and learning disorders. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 05/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants who apply before June 6, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52652": {
      "title": "Extension Faculty",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Extension Faculty - 4-H Youth Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Extension Faculty - 4-H Youth Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001444P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Extension Faculty - 4-H Youth Development Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Agricultural & Life Sciences Primary Unit Northern District Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Extension Faculty Position Control Number 1463 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 10/14/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Senior Instructor Extension Type Associate Extension Educator/Instructor Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Northern District is seeking applications for a fiscal year Extension Faculty Senior Instructor, Non-tenure track, of 4-H Youth Development. The Senior Instructor will provide leadership in 4-H Youth Development and in 4-H Youth programming. The position will provide support and extension outreach in Latah and surrounding North Central Idaho Area sub-region within the Northern Extension District. The position will provide leadership, guidance, and management to the 4-H Youth Development program in Latah County and will collaborate with Extension personnel across program and county lines plus actively participate on State 4-H teams and committees. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/extension/county/latah Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 0 Scholarship & Creative Activity 0 Outreach & Extension 95% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree related to education or youth development is required by date of hire. Experience designing, implementing, and evaluating educational programs that respond to local needs. Experience working directly with youth and adult audiences and collaborating with community organizations to provide educational experiences for program audiences. Experience incorporating audience needs and community input into program planning and delivery. Experience teaching, facilitating problem solving, communicating with varied audiences, managing conflict, building professional relationships, and supporting leadership development. Experience working as part of a team, coordinating Extension programming, and conducting marketing and promotional activities for 4-H programs. Experience communicating through oral presentations, written materials, active listening, and public speaking. Experience recruiting, training, coordinating, and supporting volunteers. Experience using technology and computer applications in program planning, delivery, communication, and evaluation. Preferred Qualifications A master’s degree in an applicable field of study. Experience in 4-H Youth Development through Extension work or other professional roles. Familiarity with Latah County and the surrounding area through residence, work, education, or community involvement. Experience with fundraising, grant writing, and cost-recovery activities. Experience working with mass media, including television, internet-based platforms, radio, and newspapers. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Work a flexible schedule, including some weekends Must: possess a valid driver’s license. Physical ability to lift, carry and/or otherwise move 50 lbs. Posting Information Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by October 3, 2026 will receive first consideration. Along with your on-line application, write a letter of qualification addressing how you meet the required and preferred qualifications listed. In addition, your application materials must include a CV, names & contact information for at least three (3) professional references, and unofficial transcripts. IMPORTANT : To be considered, your “Letter of Qualification” must address EACH of the minimum qualifications, including pertinent education and/or experience. In addition, to improve your ranking during the evaluation process, address as many of the Preferred Qualifications as possible. Information on a resume will not be accepted as a substitute for submitting a Letter of Qualification. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Transcripts Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
