    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52407": {
      "title": "Lifeguard",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Lifeguard Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lifeguard Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002189P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Lifeguard Location Moscow Division/College Auxiliary Services Department Administrative Operations FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $13.00 - $15.00 per hour depending on experience Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary This position requires that the employee work flexible shifts. This may include early morning, evenings, weekends and holidays. Employees are responsible for finding their own substitutes for scheduled shifts; are expected to work rentals and swim meets; and are expected to work together as a team. Position Responsibilities Position Summary Primary responsibility is to safeguard the lives of individuals in the University of Idaho Swim Center and prevent accidents through knowledge of lifesaving, proper use of equipment, and awareness and responsibility. Lifeguards can plan on working during operational hours, special events and rentals. Employees are expected to greet the public in a courteous manner and serve as an information source for aquatic related inquiries. This part-time position is available through the academic year and summer. Responsibilities Job Duty Function Safeguard the lives of patrons of the University of Idaho Swim Center by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Maintaining current American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification and current American Red Cross CPR :PR Certification; Maintaining constant surveillance of patrons in the facility; Acting immediately and appropriately to secure safety of patrons in the event of emergency; Providing emergency care and treatment as required until the arrival of emergency medical services; Attending all In-Services meetings/trainings. Percentage Of Time 85% Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Support the University of Idaho Swim Center by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Maintaining thorough knowledge of pool operations and programs; Establishing and maintaining good public relations with the community; Presenting a professional appearance and attitude at all times; Preparing and maintaining appropriate activity reports; Promoting all facility programs. Percentage Of Time 10% Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Contributing to team effort by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Performing various maintenance duties as directed to maintain a clean and safe facility; Performing other job-related duties as assigned. Percentage Of Time 5% Essential/Marginal Marginal Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Must possess: Current American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification or equivalent; Current American Red Cross CPR :PR Certification; Skill in the application of life guarding surveillance and rescue techniques. Preferred Qualifications Experience working as a lifeguard. Previous work experience that demonstrates ability to: Work well with public; Communicate effectively; Enforce regulations in a fair, impartial and polite manner; Work effectively as a member of a team; Exercise good judgment, both with public relations and emergency situations; Gain knowledge of safety rules and regulations and possesses willingness to enforce them; Provide good customer service. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 08/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed at regular intervals until all positions are filled. Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51161 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires a current American Red Cross Lifeguard Certification or equivalent. Do you meet this requirement? Yes No * It is a requirement of this position to possess a current American Red Cross CPR:PR Certification.  Do you meet this requirement? Yes No * A requirement for this position is possessing skills in the application of lifeguarding surveillance and rescue techniques. Please provide examples on how you meet this requirement. (Open Ended Question) Please address as many other preferred qualifications as you are able to. (Open Ended Question) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
