    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52112": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Clinical Services",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Assistant Director of Clinical Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Clinical Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005368P Position Title Assistant Director of Clinical Services Division/College Student Affairs Department Counseling and Mental Health Center Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The Counseling and Mental Health Center Assistant Director of Clinical Services provides strategic leadership, clinical oversight and administrative management for the university of Idaho’s Counseling and Mental Health Center ( CMHC ) clinical services. This position ensures the delivery of high-quality, ethical, responsive and evidence-based behavioral health services to students. This position supervises clinical staff, oversees clinical operations, ensures compliance with applicable laws and accreditation standards and collaborates with campus and community partners to promote student well-being. Position Overview Under the direction of the CMHC Executive Director, the Assistant Director of Clinical Services oversees clinical operations, crisis response, clinical staff supervision, policy development, compliance with applicable laws and professional standards, outreach programming and assessment of counseling services. The position collaborates extensively with campus partners to foster a comprehensive, campus-wide approach to student mental health. The Assistant Director of Clinical Services has a key role promoting accessible mental health services to the campus community and ensuring that those services conform with best practices in the field. In addition to the Assistant Director’s administrative role, clinical responsibilities include direct service to clients, crisis coverage, outreach and consultation to the campus community, liaison work with campus partners and after-hours response to campus events. Unit URL Counseling and Mental Health Center | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Five years providing mental health service for young adults Three years working with faculty, staff or students in higher education Supervisory experience Demonstrated experience managing projects effectively and meeting deadlines Required Education Master’s or Doctoral degree in Clinical, Counseling, Educational Psychology, Social Work or Professional Counseling Required Other Must be licensed in one of the following: Clinical, Counseling or Educational Psychologist Licensed Clinical Social Worker Licensed Clinical Professional Counselor Current independent clinical licensure (e.g., Ph.D, Psy.D, EdD, LCPC , LCSW ) in Idaho or able to obtain at the time of hire. Additional Preferred Demonstrated experience in management or leadership at a mental health clinic One or more years of supervisory or administrative leadership experience Demonstrated experience with crisis intervention and risk assessment Demonstrated skills in providing services to students Experience in a college or university counseling center Three years of supervisory experience Five years of experience as a licensed provider of clinical services Experience working on a multidisciplinary clinical staff Demonstrated experience in a leadership role with professional ethics, legal issues and risk management Demonstrated experience with mental health law and professional ethics Degree in Psychology from an APA accredited program Master’s Degree in Social Work from a CSWE accredited program Master’s Degree in Professional Counseling from a CACREP accredited program Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $90,000  or higher depending on experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/13/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To be considered your “Letter of Qualification” must address each of the required qualifications. Additionally, please provide information in support of your application regarding the preferred qualifications as relevant. For 1st consideration, please apply by September 1, 2026 Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
