    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52305": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Health Informatics, Quality &amp; Compliance Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Health Informatics, Quality & Compliance Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005391P Position Title Health Informatics, Quality & Compliance Manager Division/College Student Affairs Department Student Benefits, Health & Wellness Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The Health Informatics, Quality & Compliance Manager provides leadership for the information systems, regulatory infrastructure, quality management programs, accreditation readiness, and continuous improvement efforts supporting Student Health Services. The position integrates health information technology, operational analytics, quality improvement, compliance monitoring, policy administration, and organizational performance measurement into a coordinated system that supports clinical excellence, patient safety, regulatory compliance, and strategic decision-making. Position Overview The Health Informatics, Quality & Compliance Manager provides strategic leadership for Student Health Services’ electronic health record systems, health information governance, quality improvement, regulatory compliance, accreditation readiness, policy management, clinical analytics, and continuous organizational improvement. The position serves as the primary administrator of the Electronic Health Record ( EHR ) and is responsible for optimizing technology, data, workflows, and reporting systems that support high-quality patient care and organizational decision-making. The position also leads organizational efforts related to healthcare compliance, accreditation, quality improvement, policy administration, risk mitigation, and regulatory readiness. Working collaboratively with medical, behavioral health, administrative, and business leadership, the Health Informatics, Quality & Compliance Manager develops systems that ensure Student Health Services operates efficiently, safely, and in compliance with federal, state, university, and accreditation requirements. This position serves as the primary liaison with the Electronic Health Record vendor and provides oversight of outsourced credentialing and other compliance-related vendors to ensure contractual performance, operational effectiveness, and regulatory compliance. Unit URL Vandal Health Clinic | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Five years of progressively responsible experience in healthcare administration, health informatics, quality improvement, compliance, or healthcare operations Experience administering Electronic Health Record systems Experience developing healthcare reports and operational dashboards Experience with healthcare regulations and accreditation standards Experience leading organizational improvement initiatives Experience managing projects involving multiple stakeholders Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Health Informatics, Healthcare Administration, Public Health, Information Systems, Nursing, Health Information Management, Business Administration, or a closely related field. 4 additional years of experience, for a total of 9 years, may replace the need for a Bachelor’s degree Required Other None Additional Preferred Master’s degree in Health Informatics, Healthcare Administration ( MHA ), Public Health ( MPH ), Business Administration ( MBA ), or a related field Experience in ambulatory healthcare or student health services Experience with Medicat or comparable Electronic Health Record systems Experience with AAAHC accreditation Experience with healthcare quality improvement methodologies Experience with healthcare compliance and policy administration Experience working in higher education Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range 58,689.00 + DOE Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To be considered your “Letter of Qualification” must address each of the required qualifications. Additionally, please provide information in support of your application regarding the preferred qualifications as relevant. For 1st consideration, please apply by August 17, 2026 Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
