    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52494": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Energy Institute",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Executive Director, Energy Institute Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Executive Director, Energy Institute Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005413P Position Title Executive Director, Energy Institute Division/College College of Engineering Department College of Engineering Admin Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview As the state’s land-grant university, the University of Idaho develops solutions for complex problems facing our society. The university is establishing the Energy Institute to produce the next generation of energy leaders focused on the importance of agile energy portfolio analysis and transitions. In collaboration with industry partners, the institute will strengthen the nation’s energy future and workforce talent pipeline by integrating robust engineering design coursework and research into regional energy solutions. With partnerships across the region, the Energy Institute performs multi-discipline research that supports clean, reliable, affordable energy while delivering energy literacy education for students and professionals. The Executive Director of the Energy Institute will provide institutional vision, strategy, and leadership in educational programming, research innovation, workforce development, outreach, special projects, and advocacy in the domain of energy. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Engineering in collaboration with the Office of the President, the Executive Director will provide strategic leadership in developing and recommending key goals and actions to advance energy literacy and awareness, practical solutions to gain energy independence, and sustainable (safe, reliable, economical, renewable, clean) access to energy resources. The Executive Director will work closely with an academic leadership committee, an industry advisory board, faculty, and staff to identify, develop, implement, and promote energy programming that advances the core values and strategic priorities of the university in keeping with the needs of the energy industry. Unit URL https://www.uidaho.edu/engr Position Qualifications Required Experience 15 years of progressive leadership experience in the energy industry, utilities, or closely related organizations Building partnerships and coalitions resulting in shared actions and outcomes Experience influencing change in a complex, decentralized organization with sizeable budget, scope, and personnel Proposal development leading to external funding Leading teams to completion of project objectives on scope, on schedule, and on budget Experience with utility operating environment, including regulatory, environmental, and workforce issues Experience in the energy sector and/or energy discipline and commitment to championing energy-related causes Collaborating with multiple entities across different sectors to deepen the public’s understanding and appreciation of energy production, research, and security Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in engineering from an ABET accredited university Master’s Degree in engineering, business administration or energy studies from an accredited university Required Other Professional Engineer (PE) license from Idaho or ability to obtain an Idaho PE license within the first year of hire Completion of, or ability to complete, the University of Idaho Energy Executive Course or similar program within the first year of hire Additional Preferred Experience Demonstrated leadership of teams without direct supervisory oversight Demonstrated skills in negotiation and conflict resolution Experience with surveys, data collection, data analysis, and data visualization Technical knowledge and skills related to energy, utilities, engineering, energy economics, etc. Electric power industry experience Non-profit board leadership experience Experience should include industry, higher education, or government leadership – or a combination thereof Recognized, high-level influence with a deep understanding of key issues in the energy sector Experience with the integration of nuclear power generation into electric transmission and distribution systems Education PhD or terminal degree in energy, engineering, business administration, or economics or master’s degree with 25 years in the energy industry Experience working or collaborating in higher education Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $176,807 annually or more depending on experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding This position is contingent upon the continuation of work and/or funding. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Posting Date 08/20/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by September 3, 2026 will receive first consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
