    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52075": {
      "title": "Shop Stores Specialist II",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Shop Stores Specialist II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Shop Stores Specialist II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005363P Position Title Shop Stores Specialist II Division/College College of Science Department Chemistry Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The Department of Chemistry seeks a highly motivated individual to lead Chemstores operations, which serves the State-wide University research and teaching community. This position works independently, ensuring all aspects of operations are performed at the highest standards of Safety, State and Federal Guidelines, while also working closely with the Department manager, Safety and outside Vendors to provide best pricing, products and service to our University members. Position Overview The position performs routine manual and moderately complex clerical and physical work in a general warehouse or stockroom. The position is the first contact for customers at the Shop Store and has a special emphasis on providing leadership and training to others and the fiscal and administrative support for the Store. This is an essential position that may be called upon in the event of an emergency and/or university closure. Duties may include: Provide customer support Research and procure items Track and organize inventory and reorder as needed Handle, store and transport hazardous materials Receive, inventory, prepare for issue, and verify condition and accuracy of goods Ensure timely delivery of products Review and verify invoices and approve payment Review and send billing costs to work orders and projects Review and reconcile purchasing card activity Provide support and supervision to other staff Other duties as assigned Unit URL https://www.uidaho.edu/sci/chem Position Qualifications Required Experience Three years performing retail or warehouse duties, including receiving, storing, inventorying, and distributing materials, and providing customer service Experience researching and procuring materials, supplies and equipment Using computer software and applications for word processing, email, and internet searches. Reviewing financial documents to ensure compliance with policies, laws and regulations Providing instruction, participating in or leading a team, or delegating duties and responsibilities to others Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other None Additional Preferred Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Chemistry, or Biology (Bachelor’s degree preferred). Verbal and written communication skills Experience with U of I computer software including Banner, FAMIS and Chrome River. Safety training or certification in hazardous chemicals and materials handling Knowledge of chemistry and/or biology Knowledge and understanding of state and federal rules and procedures regarding hazardous materials storage and handling Ability to prioritize and work independently, as well as working rapidly and accurately under pressure Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to: Work closely, handling sealed and open hazardous materials containers Wear necessary Personal Protective Equipment to work with chemicals Bend, stoop, stand, kneel Lift and carry or otherwise move up to 80 pounds as needed Degree Requirement N/A: No degree requirement Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range $50,000 annually or higher depending upon education and experience Type of Appointment Academic Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding This position is contingent upon the continuation of work and/or funding. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Position will remain open until a pool of suitable candidates is identified. Please include how you meet the required qualifications and any of the preferred qualifications in your Letter of Application . Applications received by July 23, 2026 will receive first consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
