    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51644": {
      "title": "Campus and Event Safety/Security Officer (Boise)",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Campus and Event Safety/Security Officer (Boise) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus and Event Safety/Security Officer (Boise) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002168P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Campus and Event Safety/Security Officer (Boise) Location Boise Division/College DFA Operations Department Security FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $20.00 per hour Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary Available shifts would typically be between the hours of 5:00 PM–5:00 AM These hours may vary depending on operational need. Position Responsibilities Position Summary This position oversees and implements university safety and security policies to create a safe and secure environment for the university community both day-to-day and during event operations. This position also plays a key role in establishing and strengthening relationships with on-campus and off-campus stakeholders through providing exemplary customer service. May be called upon in the event of an emergency and/or university closure. Duties may include: Conduct general security patrol on campus and at events and report emergencies to university, city or state officials Assist with Safe Walks, extra patrol requests, building lockouts and on-call notifications Enforce university alcohol policies Monitor access control, check credentials, check tickets and enforce clear bag requirements Other duties as assigned Responsibilities Job Duty Function Implement event-related safety and security policies at events on campus by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Operating metal detectors and executing the metal detection screening process Enforcing university alcohol policies at events, including verifying age requirements and wrist banding patrons Enforcing access control at events by checking credentials, tickets, etc. Enforcing university clear bag requirements and checking bags as necessary Conducting general security patrol at events and reporting any emergencies to the necessary university, city or state officials Percentage Of Time 40% Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Provide 24-hour campus security services by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Providing security services across campus as assigned including campus patrols, Safe Walks, extra patrol requests, building lockouts, on-call notifications, etc. Keeping a daily activity log Reporting emergencies to the necessary university, city and state officials Percentage Of Time 40% Essential/Marginal Essential Job Duty Function Contribute to the team effort by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Accepting additional responsibilities and assignments as directed Making recommendations and assisting in the optimal use of university resources Percentage Of Time 20% Essential/Marginal Marginal Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Using computer software and applications including word-processing software, spreadsheets, email and internet Working in a team environment to accomplish shared goals Following documented policies and procedures Must be at least 18 years old Must be able to work a non-standard schedule to meet the needs of the department Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of safety and security operations and best practices One year experience as a safety/security officer Demonstrated competence with written and verbal communication Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to: Move around and between venues throughout the workday Carry, lift or otherwise move items weighing up to 40 pounds occasionally Bend, stoop, shovel and be comfortable working at significant heights Traverse any part of campus including asphalt, sidewalks, grass, dirt, playgrounds, etc . Sit and stand for extended periods of time Work in inclement weather conditions Posting Information Posting Date 05/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will be reviewed until all positions are filler. Please submit a current resume, and references (last 3 supervisors). Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/50168 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Are you at least 18 years of age? yes no Please describe how you meet the qualification of using computer software and applications. (Open Ended Question) This position requires experience working in a team environment .  Please describe/explain how you meet this requirement. (Open Ended Question) A requirement of this position is following documented policies and procedures. Please describe how you meet this requirement. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
