    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52500": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Data Governance Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Data Governance Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005414P Position Title Data Governance Manager Division/College General Library Department General Library Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The University of Idaho is building the data foundation that will power research, student success and operational excellence for years to come. The Data Governance Manager ensures the foundation is trustworthy by establishing policies and practices that make data a reliable institutional asset. This role reports to the Chief Data and AI Officer with a direct line to executive leadership, institutional visibility and the opportunity to shape how a public R1 research university governs and uses data at a pivotal moment in its modernization. Candidates energized by building programs from the ground up, working across organizational boundaries and making complex systems work are encouraged to apply. Position Overview The Data Governance Manager leads the development, implementation and ongoing maturation of enterprise data governance at the University of Idaho. Reporting to the Chief Data and AI Officer, this position is responsible for establishing the frameworks, policies, standards and institutional processes that ensure university data is accurate, accessible, secure and used responsibly across academic, administrative and research functions. This role operates at the intersection of policy, people and technology. Translating governance principles into operational practice across a complex, decentralized institution , the Data Governance Manager works closely with data stewards, IT teams, compliance and legal counsel, institutional research and senior leadership to build a governance atmosphere that supports data-informed decision-making and regulatory compliance. The position entails equal parts strategic thinking, stakeholder facilitation and operational follow-through. Duties may include: Developing and maintaining the university’s enterprise data governance framework, policies and standards Facilitating the Data Governance Committee and associated working groups Defining and operationalizing data ownership, stewardship and accountability structures across institutional data domains Managing the enterprise data catalog and driving metadata standards and data quality practices Partnering with IT, compliance, legal and academic units to ensure governance alignment with regulatory requirements Leading data literacy and governance education efforts across the institution Supporting the CDAO in developing and communicating institutional data strategy Other duties as assigned Unit URL Office of Information Technology | University of Idaho University of Idaho Library | University of Idaho Library Home Position Qualifications Required Experience 3 years of experience in data governance, data management, information management or a closely related field Demonstrated experience facilitating cross-functional teams and building consensus across stakeholders with competing priorities Experience developing or implementing policies, frameworks or standards in a complex organizational environment Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Information Management, Business, Public Administration, Computer Science or a related field, or 4 additional years of experience (for a total of 7 years) Required Other None Additional Preferred 5 or more years of experience in data governance, enterprise data management, or institutional data strategy Certification in data governance or data management (e.g., CDMP , DAMA , or similar) Graduate degree in a relevant field Experience with: Higher education institutions, including familiarity with shared governance structures and constituent-sensitive data environments Regulatory frameworks applicable to higher education data ( FERPA , HIPAA , GLBA or federal grant compliance) Enterprise data catalog platforms and metadata management tooling Cloud-based data platforms and lakehouse architecture concepts (Databricks and Unity Catalog preferred) ERP data structures in student, HR or finance domains (Banner/Ellucian preferred) Data quality frameworks and data quality tooling Building and facilitating governance committees, working groups or advisory bodies Developing data stewardship programs, including steward recruitment, training and ongoing engagement Translating governance requirements for both technical teams and non-technical institutional audiences AI governance frameworks and the intersection of data governance with machine learning and analytics use cases Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of application Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $85,000 annually or more depending on experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 08/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open until filled. Applications received by 09/21/2026 will be given first consideration. All applicants are asked to submit their resume, a letter of qualification , and three professional references within the application. The letter of qualification should address all of the required and preferred qualifications for the position. References should include recent direct supervisors. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52294": {
      "title": "Soil/Crop Technical Planner",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Soil/Crop Technical Planner Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Soil/Crop Technical Planner Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002202P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title Soil/Crop Technical Planner Location Off Campus Location - Opportunities across Idaho Division/College College of Agricultural & Life Sciences Department Soils and Water Systems FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $28 an hour or higher depending on experience Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary Schedule will be determined upon hiring. The identified hire(s) will work no more than 20 hours per week. End date for work is undetermined Position Responsibilities Position Summary This position is available through the Innovative Agriculture and Marketing Partnership ( IAMP ) project at the University of Idaho. The IAMP project offers per acre incentive payments for producers to adopt conservation practices within their cropping systems, see http://iamp.uidaho.edu. Implementing partners including Idaho soil & water conservation districts, The Nature Conservancy, Desert Mountain Grassfed Beef, Nez Perce Tribe, and Coeur d’Alene Tribe work directly with enrolling producers in the program. Potential funded conservation practices include various nutrient management strategies such as reduced synthetic fertilizers or the replacement of synthetic fertilizers with organic (e.g. compost) sources, 4R strategies, reduced and no-tillage practices, conservation crop rotation strategies which incorporate more legume crops into a crop rotation or through inter-cropping strategies, cover cropping, grazing, and biochar addition. Producers enter a multi-year contract to implement a cropping plan that includes one or more of these practices. Annual verification of implemented practice and assessments are conducted with each producer to evaluate compliance issues with the contract. Producers are encouraged to engage in novel marketing opportunities that recognize and promote climate-smart attributes associated with the commodities grown in the program. This posting may hire more than one Responsibilities Job Duty Function Contribute to the overall success of the Innovative Agriculture and Marketing Partnership (IAMP) project by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Assist implementing partners and/or work directly with producers on developing nutrient, tillage, and cropping strategies which implement conservation practices on specific agricultural fields. Assist planners and/or work directly through a two-phased application process that includes compliance documentation as required by the USDA to ensure producers do not receive duplicate payments from multiple USDA programs for the same practice on the same field. Perform advanced compliance modeling to ensure unintended environmental impacts are not occurring within an enrolled field, including soil erosion modeling ( RUSLE , WEPS ) and nutrient losses ( INTRA ). Train, assist, and/or be directly involved in end-of-year meetings with producers to evaluate the impact of implemented practices on crop performance, profitability, soil carbon, and greenhouse gas emissions. Participate on a Review Advisory Committee that provides advice and evaluation on potential contracts and any compliance issues that are associated with grower contracts and agreements. Participate in meetings with IAMP project management and implementing partner meetings associated with technical issues of the grant. Attend and work with UI Extension on providing materials and information for field days. Assist in communication and engagement with producers on marketing opportunities for the commodities grown through the IAMP project. Percentage Of Time 100% Essential/Marginal Essential Position Qualifications Required Qualifications A Bachelor’s degree in soil science, agronomy, crop science, agroecology, biological systems engineering, or closely related field relevant to the project, or 5 years experience as a crop or technical service provider to producers. Experience with historic and innovative cropping systems of the region Experience conducting research independently and collaborating as part of a research team Experience working on large, integrated research projects Experience preparing and delivering scientific presentations and technical reports Preferred Qualifications Knowledge and experience using RUSLE , WEPS , and INTRA tools. Experience as a cropping consultant or technical service provider. Knowledge and experience with NRCS and NRCS programs (e.g. EQIP ). Strong analytical skills. Experience with remote sensing and geospatial mapping and analysis products. Experience in soil and crop sampling. Background and interest in Extension, outreach, and/or the application of scientific information in practice. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Ability to lift 30 lbs Driver’s License Willingness to travel. Posting Information Posting Date 07/29/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please address all the minimum requirements in the Letter of Qualification. Preferential review of applicants to begin on August 5, 2026 If you would like additional information about this position, please contact Erin Brooks ebrooks@uidaho.edu Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52272 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52227": {
      "title": "**Director of Rangeland Center FRFS / CNR",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | **Director of Rangeland Center FRFS / CNR Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help **Director of Rangeland Center FRFS / CNR Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001436P Internal Posting? This Search is Open to Current University of Idaho Employees Only Recruitment Title **Director of Rangeland Center FRFS / CNR Advertising Pay Range 10% base salary stipend, summer salary to be negotiable annually with the Dean Location Moscow, Boise Primary Division/College College of Natural Resources Primary Unit Forest, Rangeland, & Fire Sciences Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Program Dir/Dist Dir/Super Position Control Number 3701 Suffix 01 Contingency Code 5 FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/17/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Negotiable (must be justified) Rank Negotiable (must be justified) Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type On-going Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary N/A Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/cnr/rangeland-center Administrative Summary The Director of the Rangeland Center serves as the administrative coordinator for the Rangeland Center, acting as the central figure in managing and enhancing all aspects of the program. As the primary point of contact, the Director ensures seamless communication and collaboration both within the program and with external partners. They will oversee and enhance the program’s strategic initiatives, research endeavors, operational effectiveness, and overall excellence, striving to elevate its standing and impact. The Director will lead, manage, and coordinate a wide range of responsibilities to ensure the program’s activities align with the college’s mission and goals. This includes fostering a supportive and dynamic environment and effective supervision for faculty, staff, and students, promoting innovative teaching methods, and advancing scholarly research. The employee will direct and manage sustainable budget practices for their program. The Director will also play a crucial role in community outreach, building strong relationships with industry partners, and advocating for the program at various levels. Job duty functions for teaching, scholarship, outreach, and leadership will be negotiated at the time of hire. This position is open to current fiscal year and academic year non-tenure track, tenure track, and tenured faculty at the ranks of assistant, associate or full professors at the University of Idaho. This administrative role is accompanied by a 10% base salary stipend. As the administrative duties occur over the entire calendar year, those on fiscal year appointment will have the duties included in their positions. Those on academic year contracts will have summer contracts negotiated annually with the dean. Contingency Description This administrative appointment or the administrative portion of the faculty appointment is temporary. Employee acknowledges and agrees that in the event there is no longer a need for the administrative assignment, as determined by University in its sole discretion, University may change this Agreement and remove the administrative salary and/or course release during the contract year and employee may return to their faculty appointment, upon 60 days written notice. Teaching & Advising TBD Scholarship & Creative Activity TBD Outreach & Extension TBD University Service & Leadership 40% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications PhD in Rangeland Ecology, Natural Resources, Environmental Science, or Plant Science Current non-tenure track, tenure track, and tenured academic year and fiscal year faculty at the ranks of assistant, associate or full professor at the University of Idaho. Experience engaging partners and stakeholders to provide leadership for the program. Preferred Qualifications Experience facilitating collaborative, broad-based, interdisciplinary research and outreach. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open to current tenure track, tenured, and non-tenure track faculty currently employed at the University of Idaho. Priority will be given to applicants who have submitted their materials by August 5th, 2026. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52650": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005435P Position Title Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development Division/College Vice Provost for Strategic Enrollment Management Department Career Services Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview Serving on the Career Services Leadership Team, the Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development is responsible for developing and maintaining partnerships with state, regional, national, and international employers to increase internships, professional experiences, graduate school, and career opportunities for UI students and graduates. The Assistant Director works with the Career Services Director, Employer Relations staff, and UI branch center directors to accomplish the following, aligning this work with the workforce and educational needs of Idaho’s employers and students: Create and implement a plan for relationship-building with employers in Idaho and the Northwest that offer professional experiences, graduate school pathways, and career positions related to UI majors and degree programs Develop and implement strategies to increase connections and networking opportunities between students and employers Assist employers in expanding their internship programs and accessing qualified internship candidates The Assistant Director also leads the department’s fundraising and development efforts through Career Services’ Distinguished Employer Partnership Program ( DEP ), and leads the department’s assessment plan by collecting employer outreach data and writing reports and recommendations based on that data. Unit URL Career Services | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Two years professional experience working in recruitment, human resources, talent management or other related experience One year of professional experience in event planning or development/fundraising Experience with program planning and implementation Experience providing presentations to small and large groups Required Education Bachelors degree Required Other Must be eligible for membership in relevant professional organizations Ability to work nonstandard hours including a flexible schedule during select mornings, evenings and weekends to address event needs Ability to travel regionally, in-state and out-of-state on a periodic basis Additional Preferred Education: Master’s degree E xperience: Professional work experience in a university career services office or employer relations role Managing career services database systems (i.e. Handshake, Symplicity, 12Twenty, CSO , or other job search databases) Technical/computer experience, including the experience using software such as Access, Excel, video conferencing programs (Zoom) and on-line survey programs (Qualtrics, SurveyMonkey, etc. Developing a process for assessment, collecting/analyzing data, and preparing reports and recommendations Skills/knowledge/Ability to: Demonstrated past success in development/fundraising efforts Strong verbal and written communication skills Ability to work effectively both as part of a team and independently to complete tasks Strong organization skills Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $55,000 or higher depending on education and experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is posted as open until filled, however, applications submitted on or before September 17, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Position will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Applicants: Please use your letter of qualification to explain in detail how your work experience, skills, and abilities meet both the required and preferred qualifications as listed in the position description. Your letter of qualification will be used to demonstrate your communication and writing skills to determine your ranking among the other applicants for this position. For resources about how to write a letter of qualification , please visit the HR website here: Applicant Resources – Careers | University of Idaho (uidaho.edu) If you would like to view a full copy of the job description, please reach out to the search coordinator at eschirmer@uidaho.edu Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
