    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52614": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Project Architect Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Project Architect Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005405P Position Title Project Architect Division/College AVP, Budget and Planning Department Architectural and Engineering Services Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview This position provides a wide range of architectural, engineering, landscape, planning, and environmental project design, and project management and administration services. Working closely with clients, architects, engineers, landscape architects, planning and design consultants, regulatory agencies, and other stakeholders, this position ensures that the university’s capital design and construction projects meet both aesthetic and functional requirements while adhering to budgetary and regulatory constraints. This position will coordinate various aspects of the project, including design development, documentation, construction oversight, and ensuring compliance with building codes, zooming regulations and other legal requirements. Duties may include: Lead capital design and construction projects from inception to completion, including developing project plans, timelines and budgets Create innovative and functional architectural, engineering, and environmental designs that meet the university’s requirements, regulatory standards and budgetary constraints Collaborate closely with clients, architects, engineers, professional consultants, contractors, regulatory agencies and other stakeholders Prepare and review planning, architectural, engineering, landscape architectural, and other proposals, drawings, specifications and construction documents, ensuring accuracy and completeness Identify and resolve design, construction, and technical issues that may arise during a project, ensuring timely and effective solutions Provide leadership and guidance to team members Other duties as assigned Unit URL University architectural planning, design and construction | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience Five years practicing architecture, engineering or landscape architecture Professional experience in one or more of the following areas: Space utilization and planning principles Cost estimating techniques Preparation of construction contracts and documents Analysis of plans and specifications for conformance with building codes and standards Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in Architecture, Architectural Engineering, Engineering or Landscape Architecture Required Other Must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Additional Preferred Current, valid State of Idaho professional registration or license in Architecture, Engineering, Landscape Architecture or eligible for reciprocal registration as provided by Idaho Code Experience on design, construction and/or project management groups that maintain and operate a system of buildings and structures in support of the strategic goals of a large institution or organization Experience using computer applications commonly used in architecture, engineering and landscape architecture (e.g., CADD , 3-D modeling and other rendering software) Physical Requirements & Working Conditions None Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $80,000 or higher, commensurate with experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 08/17/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification, current resume, and references (last 3 supervisors) no later than August 31st. In your letter of qualifications ( human-resources-letter-of-qualification-template.docx ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu . Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
