    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52568": {
      "title": "General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005328P Position Title General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Division/College Auxiliary Services Department Campus Services Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Position Overview General Technician I This position will perform general building maintenance tasks on a regular and continuing basis. It will provide general support for a variety of construction, trades, landscaping, exterior service and maintenance areas to repair and maintain university facilities and grounds. Job duties will vary widely depending on the work and projects assigned. Duties may include: Utilize basic tools and equipment Repair and maintain basic machinery, equipment and facility property Assist with routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Assist with inventory and distribution of deliveries Manually move and transfer items Participate in snow removal Other duties as assigned General Technician II This position independently performs semi-skilled maintenance and repair duties that vary widely depending on the work and projects assigned. It is responsible for inspecting, maintaining and repairing university equipment and facilities. The position will provide support for construction, maintenance and other skilled trade professionals to meet university needs. Duties may include: Perform routine maintenance and repairs to university facilities Assist trades, crafts, vendors and technical staff with construction, design and operational maintenance as needed Repair and maintain machinery, equipment and facilities Perform routine and non-routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Receive, inspect, inventory and distribute deliveries independently to appropriate entities Other duties as assigned General Technician III This position provides leadership to the General Technician team, which performs semi-skilled maintenance and repair duties for university facilities and equipment on and near the Moscow campus. The work of the team varies widely depending on the work and projects assigned. The position is responsible for planning, organizing, training and monitoring the team’s daily work activities while also performing inspection, maintenance and repair duties. Duties may include: Hire, train and supervise the General Technician team Monitor and balance workload among individual technicians Perform routine maintenance and repairs to university facilities Assist trades, crafts, vendors and technical staff with construction, design and operational maintenance as needed Repair and maintain machinery, equipment and facilities Perform routine and non-routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Receive, inspect, inventory and distribute deliveries independently to appropriate entities Other duties as assigned Unit URL Division of Finance and Administration ( DFA ) | University of Idaho Position Qualifications Required Experience General Technician I Working in a team to accomplish goals General Technician II Three years performing semi-skilled maintenance tasks General Technician III Five years performing semi-skilled maintenance tasks in custodial, landscape, construction and/or utilities trades Required Education General Technician I, II, and III High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other General Technician I, II, and III Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Be at least 18 years of age Ability to participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation which may include nonstandard business hours including evenings, weekends and holidays periodically Additional Preferred General Technician I Experience: Working in construction or building maintenance Using power tools and equipment Expressed interest in learning and acquiring skills related to building maintenance General Technician II Experience With heating and cooling system maintenance and repairs With basic components and functions of electrical systems, plumbing systems, heating ventilation systems, roofing systems, security lock systems and mechanical systems in residential type dwellings Installing carpet, sheet vinyl, luxury vinyl plank and/or ceramic tile Post-secondary education and/or license in one or more of the following areas: plumbing, electrical or HVAC General Technician III Experience With heating and cooling system maintenance and repairs With basic components and functions of electrical systems, plumbing systems, heating ventilation systems, roofing systems, security lock systems and mechanical systems in residential type dwellings Installing carpet, sheet vinyl, luxury vinyl plank and/or ceramic tile Post-secondary education and/or license in one or more of the following areas: plumbing, electrical or HVAC Physical Requirements & Working Conditions General Technician I, II, and III Must be able to: Bend, stoop and work in awkward positions for several hours at a time Climb and work from ladders, scaffolding and scissor lifts Carry, lift or otherwise move items weighing up to 50 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Degree Requirement N/A: No degree requirement Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range General Technician I $17.19 per hour or higher depending on experience. General Technician II $19.78 per hour or higher depending on experience. General Technician III $22.35 per hour or higher depending on experience. Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding This position is contingent upon the continuation of work and/or funding. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 06/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This in-person position is based in Moscow, Idaho and not offering Visa sponsorship. To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification, current resume, and references (last 3 supervisors) no later than July 6th. In your letter of qualifications ( human-resources-letter-of-qualification-template.docx ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. This description is a summary only and describes the general level of work being performed, it is not intended to be all-encompassing. The duties of a position may change from time to time based on business need. We reserve the right to add or delete duties and responsibilities at the discretion of the supervisor and/or hiring authority. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
