    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/51852": {
      "title": "Extension Educator",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001431P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Location Off Campus Location - Bear Lake County - Montpelier, Idaho Primary Division/College College of Agricultural & Life Sciences Primary Unit Eastern District Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Extension Faculty Position Control Number 1825 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/17/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type County Extension Educator/Professorial Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The University of Idaho Extension Eastern District seeks a 12-month, tenure-track Extension Educator with the rank of Assistant Professor for Bear Lake County, providing leadership for multifaceted livestock (50%), agriculture (30%), and 4-H Youth Development (20%) programs. They will collaborate closely with county partners, commissioners, and community organizations to ensure programs meet local needs and align with University and Extension priorities. The position includes conducting scholarly work (5%) and contributing to University leadership and service, including county chair duties (15%). This position receives an annual flat rate administrative stipend of $1,500 for County Chair duties. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/extension/county/bear-lake Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 0% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 80% University Service & Leadership 15% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution in animal science, agricultural science, Extension education, or a closely related discipline. The degree must be completed by the date of hire. Experience providing organizational structure and support for a variety of individuals and groups Experience in adapting research materials for effective oral and written presentations Experience recruiting, teaching, organizing and managing groups Experience using technology for program delivery, reporting and teams-based communication Preferred Qualifications Ability to work well in a team and provide effective instruction, support, and marketing for programs Previous experience working in Extension Experience in disseminating results through scholarly outlets Experience with supervising, leading, and mentoring others Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Work a flexible schedule, including some weekends Must possess a valid driver’s license. Ability to lift, carry and/or otherwise move 50 lbs. Posting Information Posting Date 06/18/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by July 18, 2026 will receive first consideration. Along with your online application, write a letter of qualification addressing how you meet the required and preferred qualifications listed. In addition, your application materials must include a CV, names & contact information for at least three (3) professional references, and unofficial transcripts. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible 