    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/49792": {
      "title": "PRN Physician",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | PRN Physician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help PRN Physician Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Classification Information Posting Number STH002165P Employee Category Student/Temporary Position Information Position Title PRN Physician Location Moscow Division/College Student Affairs Department Student Benefits, Health & Wellness FLSA Status Non-Exempt Pay Range $90 per hour + Depending on Experience Full Time/Part Time Part Time Work Schedule Summary This is an On-Call/As Needed Position. Clinic Operating Hours are Monday – Friday 8am – 5pm. Position Responsibilities Position Summary Under the direction of the Medical Director of the University of Idaho Vandal Health Clinic, provide health care to pediatric, adolescent and adult patients. This position will perform and maintain standards of care in: General Medicine Gynecology Sports Medicine Trauma Infectious Diseases including STIs Minor Surgical Skills Dermatology Women’s Health Psychosocial Medicine Responsibilities Job Duty Function Performing patient care, managing communication and recordkeeping for the clinic by: Job Duties/Responsibilities Assuming responsibility and accountability for patient care Exercising administrative judgment, assuming responsibility for decisions, consequences and results impacting patients, costs and/or quality of service Participating in peer chart reviews and passing periodic laboratory proficiency testing and quality control reviews Attending Vandal Health Clinic meetings and educational opportunities and continued self-development and professional involvement, participating in activities and educational programs of professional organizations Conducting a positive representation of the Vandal Health Clinic & University of Idaho Establishing and maintaining effective channels of communication building professional relationships with patients, physicians, co-workers, contractors and outside facilities Using equipment and materials in a safe manner, following established safety procedures, using appropriate safeguards and observing rules of safety in all on-the job activities Observing patient confidentiality Paying attention to detail Maintaining records and files Performing other duties and tasks as assigned Percentage Of Time 100 Essential/Marginal Essential Position Qualifications Required Qualifications Experience in young adult health, public health, or college health. A terminal degree (M.D., D.O.) Board certified or Board eligible Active State of Idaho Physician and Surgeon Medical License or ability to obtain by hire date Active DEA and Idaho Controlled Substances registrations or ability to obtain by hire date Basic Life Support Provider Certification upon hire Preferred Qualifications Five (5) or more years of experience as a Physician in an ambulatory setting Experience working with or knowledge of the HIPAA of 1996 and FERPA , pertaining to the release of protected health information Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/14/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide a resume and letter of qualifications listing your experience. This is a temporary appointment. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis until position is filled. Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates may be required to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Quicklink for Posting https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/49784 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
