    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52201": {
      "title": "Director of Athletic Communications",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Director of Athletic Communications Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Athletic Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005379P Position Title Director of Athletic Communications Division/College Athletics Department Athletics General Location Moscow Posting Context Statement The Director of Athletic Communications reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for External Operations and is responsible for all communications, media relations and publicity activities for the Department of Athletics, including assigned sports. The position is expected to provide and maximize positive exposure of the University of Idaho, its athletics programs, events, student-athletes, coaches and staff. Position Overview The position ensures effective external communication, branding and messaging by leading and collaborating on communication efforts within the Department of Athletics and across campus. This position advances the reputation of Idaho Vandal Athletics, the University of Idaho, and assigned unit(s) through purposeful and creative messaging. The position will work in a collaborative environment with Department of Athletics staff, teams, coaches, student-athletes and partners on and off campus to create impactful communications. This position will act within all NCAA , Big Sky Conference, HIPAA , FERPA and university rules, laws and requirements. Duties may include: Managing and hiring communications staff Managing communications budget and expenditures Write and edit a variety of content for assigned sports Maintain govandals.com, social media presence, and online communications Collaborate on data collection, insights and metrics to improve revenue digital strategy Collect and maintain statistical records for assigned sports Work with local and national media and broadcast partners to ensure accurate and timely reporting Provide consultation and writing support to department leadership Other duties as assigned Unit URL govandals.com Position Qualifications Required Experience One year performing media relations or public event organization Required Education Bachelor’s Degree in communications; four additional years of experience (for a total of five years) may substitute for a Bachelor’s Degree Required Other None Additional Preferred Experience working in collegiate athletics Experience working directly with coaching staffs and teams Strong writer and copy editor Experience with video production and graphic design in Adobe Creative Suite Knowledge and understanding of NCAA rules and regulations regarding compliance issues Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to work in an environment with continual interruptions and outside noise Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of application Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $55-65K Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 07/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by 08/04/26 will receive first consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
