    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52625": {
      "title": "Director of Broadcast Production",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Director of Broadcast Production Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Director of Broadcast Production Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005427P Position Title Director of Broadcast Production Division/College Athletics Department Athletics General Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview The Director of Broadcast Production will oversee all production of Idaho Vandal Athletics video and digital broadcasts, managing the delivery of content and programming for ESPN , the Big Sky Conference, regional and national television and other official department channels and opportunities. This position will also oversee a large group of gameday staff and student interns. Key responsibilities include scheduling student and freelance crew, preparing production documents, shooting footage to appear in broadcasts and equipment set-up. The position reports directly to the Director of Athletic Digital Content and Productions. Duties may include directing and producing live events; producing video for marketing and recruiting purposes and other duties associated with live production of events and content creation. Unit URL govandals.com Position Qualifications Required Experience Experience with remote and studio production editing, camera operation and audio Experience using digital editing software in a work environment Experience using video graphic methods, techniques, processes and equipment Required Education None Required Other Ability to work nonstandard business hours, including weekends and holidays Additional Preferred Bachelor’s degree in broadcast journalism, video production, Radio/TV/Film, communications, or related field Master’s degree preferred Experience directing and/or producing in-venue shows or live broadcasts, as well as the ability to create high-impact videos from ideation through postproduction Experience with digital video hardware, software, infrastructure and personnel necessary for live and on-demand HD sports production, transmission and archiving preferred Experience operating and utilizing HD Camera Systems, fiber optic transport systems, broadcast audio systems and replay systems Demonstrate experience in content development, shooting and postproduction for videoboards and/or social media platforms Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and coordinate with internal and external stakeholders Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, meet production deadlines, and adapt to changing circumstances in a fast-paced live production environment Demonstrated interest in or experience with collegiate athletics Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Working outdoors in all weather conditions Working in small spaces and platforms exposed to heights Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of application Posting Information FLSA Status Exempt Employee Category Exempt Pay Range $50,000-$55,000 annually Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 08/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by September 3, 2026 will receive first consideration for review. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicat