    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52363": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Custodian I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Custodian I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005208P Position Title Custodian I Division/College Facilities Management Department Facilities Admin Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview The position is responsible for maintaining clean and orderly facilities for students, faculty, staff and visitors. As part of a self-directed team, the position will take initiative to schedule cleaning and maintenance activities. Duties may include: Perform basic cleaning, sanitization and trash collection in and around residences halls and university buildings Maintain cleaning equipment and supplies Notify occupants of cleaning and floor maintenance schedules Maintain clean and clear walkways, ensuring they are free of debris, litter, snow and ice Respond to emergencies and assist other departments when needed to ensure optimum service Ensure that assigned rooms and buildings are opened and locked as scheduled Assist with training new employees Other duties as assigned Unit URL https://www.uidaho.edu/facility-services Position Qualifications Required Experience Performing cleaning tasks Working in a team-oriented environment Required Education None Required Other Be at least 18 years of age Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Additional Preferred Experience operating industrial high-speed cleaning equipment; performing minor maintenance on custodial equipment; and explaining the use and maintenance of custodial equipment Expressed interest in learning and acquiring skills related to custodial services Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to: Climb ladders, bend and stoop Lift, carry or otherwise move items weighing up to 50 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of application Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range $16.00 per hour - $16.80 per hour includes 5% shift differential pay Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1.0 Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Posting Date 03/23/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The priority consideration date for applications is 4/20/2026. Applications after that date will be reviewed on an ongoing basis until positions are filled. Shifts available: 4:00am-12:00pm, 4:00pm-1:00am, 7:00pm-5:30am Full-time, 40 hours per week When entering employment history, be sure to include all past work experience relevant to the duties of this position in the Employment Experience section of the application. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you at least 18 years of age? yes no * Describe fully how you meet each required qualification of this position. (experience, education and required other)  Only applicants who demonstrate that they meet all required qualifications in their written application are eligible to be considered for the position. (Open Ended Question) Describe how you meet any of the preferred qualifications for this position. (Open Ended Question) * Describe any work history related to the described duties of this position. (Open Ended Question) * The University of Idaho has elected not to sponsor new H1-B visas. No visa sponsorship is available for this position. If hired, can you show proof of authorization to work in the United States? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
