    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52635": {
      "title": "General Technician I",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | General Technician I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help General Technician I Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Internal Posting? Posting Number SP005432P Position Title General Technician I Division/College Facilities Management Department Facilities Management-Shops/Misc. Location Moscow Posting Context Statement Position Overview This position will perform general building maintenance tasks on a regular and continuing basis. It will provide general support for a variety of construction, trades, landscaping, exterior service and maintenance areas to repair and maintain university facilities and grounds. Job duties will vary widely depending on the work and projects assigned. Duties may include: Utilize basic tools and equipment Repair and maintain basic machinery, equipment and facility property Assist with routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Assist with inventory and distribution of deliveries Manually move and transfer items Participate in snow removal Other duties as assigned Unit URL Facilities | DFA | University of Idaho (uidaho.edu) https://www.uidaho.edu/dfa/facilities Position Qualifications Required Experience Working in a team to accomplish goals Required Education High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other Possess a valid driver’s license and the ability to meet university requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Be at least 18 years of age Additional Preferred Experience: Working in construction or building maintenance Using power tools and equipment Expressed interest in learning and acquiring skills related to building maintenance Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to: Bend, stoop and work in awkward positions for several hours at a time Climb and work from ladders, scaffolding and scissor lifts Carry, lift or otherwise move items weighing up to 50 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Degree Requirement Listed degree qualification is required at time of application Posting Information FLSA Status Non-Exempt Employee Category Classified Pay Range Commensurate with Experience Type of Appointment Fiscal Year FTE 1. Full Time/Part Time Full Time Funding A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants First review date 9/17/26. Applications after that date will be reviewed on an ongoing basis until positions are filled. When entering employment history, be sure to include all past work experience relevant to the duties of this position in the Employment Experience section of the application. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Are you at least 18 years of age? yes no * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No * Describe how you meet all required qualifications of this position. (Open Ended Question) Describe how you meet any of the preferred qualifications for this position. (Open Ended Question) * Describe any work history related to the described duties of this position. (Open Ended Question) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
